rls at risk for urinary tract infection</article-title><source>Arch Pediatr Adolesc Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>154</volume><fpage>386</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10768678</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lockhart</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewander</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cimini</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Josephson</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Linakis</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of urinary gram stain for detection of urinary tract infection in infants</article-title><source>Ann Emerg Med</source><year>1995</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>31</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7528483</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0196-0644(95)70351-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lohr</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Use of routine urinalysis in making a presumptive diagnosis of urinary tract infection in children</article-title><source>Pediatr Infect Dis J</source><year>1991</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>646</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1923675</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldsmith</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Campos</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of urine dipstick, microscopy, and culture for the detection of bacteriuria in children</article-title><source>Clin Pediatr (Phila)</source><year>1990</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>214</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2331830</pub-id></citat